\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Sharing.

\series default
 A project is private to you until you share it —
 like a Google Doc.
 File\SpecialChar menuseparator
Share project\SpecialChar ldots
 (or the share button next to the project in the file browser) invites people by username or e-mail address as
\emph on
 viewers
\emph default
 or 
\emph on
 editors
\emph default
,
 and can turn on a link that anyone signed in can use.
 Someone invited by e-mail gets access the moment they sign in with Google.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Presence.

\series default
 Everybody who has the document open appears as a small avatar in the status bar,
 and their cursors and selections show in the text in their colour.
 Click an avatar to jump to where that person is editing.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Saving.

\series default
 There is no Save button:
 every change goes to the server as you type and is written to the
\family typewriter
 .lyx
\family default
 file a moment later (the status bar says 
\emph on
 All changes saved
\emph default
).
 If you open the same file in desktop \SpecialChar LyX
 and save it there,
 OverLyX picks up the change.
 Working offline is fine too —
 edits are kept in the browser and merge when you are back.
\end_layout

